   ANALYSIS ARCHITECTURE
 - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -

   Layer 1 (Strings)  : Runtime reflection dump of the client's own decryptor
                        -> 7,806 / 7,806 strings recovered

   Layer 2 (Code enc) : Keystream derivation reproduced statically
                        - target section identified by name-prefix product
                        - seed evolved from sibling sections' content hash
                          (this doubles as the anti-tamper mechanism)
                        -> 15,380 encrypted method bodies decrypted

   Layer 3 (VM)       : Three sub-layers separated and each broken
                        (a) RSA-2048 / PKCS#1 v1.5 envelope
                            - modulus = FieldRva(128B) || base64(128B), e=65537
                            - 2,948 blocks, every block valid PKCS#1 v1.5,
                              padding length exactly 8 -> fixed chunking proven
                        (b) position-dependent stream XOR
                            - plain[i] = cipher[i] ^ (byte)(seed ^ i)
                            - entropy 7.9997 -> 6.7565
                        (c) self-describing Ascii85 method tokens
                            - token -> Ascii85 -> XOR -> scrambled int64
                              -> VM stream offset
                            - runtime probe vs offline recomputation: 7/7 exact
                            - encoding proven fully invertible
                        => 722,260 bytes of VM bytecode as readable plaintext
                           (3,917 member records, 7,107 printable strings)

   Layer 4 (Cipher)   : Custom TEA variant fully specified
                        - 32-bit block / 80-bit key / ECB / 12 rounds
                        - S-box round function with 10-byte key schedule
                        - 5-stage cascade, per-stage key+IV from DeriveBytes KDF

